      <abstract>
        <para>The Linux Security Module (LSM) framework in &productname; provides a modular architecture that enforces Mandatory Access Control (MAC) alongside standard Linux permissions. By using LSMs like Yama to restrict sensitive system calls such as ptrace, administrators can harden system security, prevent unauthorized memory inspection, and block lateral movement between user processes without sacrificing system flexibility.</para>
